mutant: m076_compaction_skips_refresh_after_publish
target: internal/ingest/orchestrator/compact_deletes.go
failure-mode: |
  A compaction chunk that published a generation does not refresh the
  leader's catalog view, so the next chunk of the same pass reads a
  segment's replaced generation and rewrites from it. PublishGeneration's
  source check refuses the publish as corruption and the leader exits;
  without that check the new generation would silently resurrect the
  rows the earlier chunk removed. Removing the source check alone is an
  equivalent mutant (a replaced source is already deleted, so the
  missing-generation check fires), so this models the bug it guards.
expected-detection: |
  The layer 3 oracle: a pass whose tombstones span more than one chunk
  (cap 4) rewrites a segment twice, the leader fails loud on the second
  publish, and the run reports an unexpected leader error.
expected-tier: disagg
tiers: disagg

